//@version=6
//
// Trend Signal (Honest) — simple BUY/SELL from the one rule that measured profitable
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT THIS IS
//   Close vs a long moving average, with a hysteresis band to cut whipsaw. That's it.
//   BUY when price closes above the band, SELL (to cash) when it closes below.
//   No oscillators, no volume filter, no volatility filter, no confluence stack.
//
// WHY IT IS THIS SIMPLE — THIS IS THE IMPORTANT PART
//   Built 2026-09-06 after measuring three richer designs on BTC + ETH daily bars
//   (2019-2026, Coinbase, 0.54% round-trip cost, non-overlapping trades):
//
//     1. Fade the volatility bands (mean reversion)     -> PF 0.42-0.66. Loses.
//        Systematically shorted a 20x bull market.
//     2. Volatility-compression breakout ("coiled spring") -> PF 0.24-0.46. Loses.
//        And its PREMISE is false: after vol compression the subsequent 5-day
//        absolute move is SMALLER, not bigger (t = -2.46, p = 0.014). Low vol
//        begets low vol. The "squeeze must release" idea did not survive contact
//        with the data at this horizon.
//     3. Volatility regime as an OVERLAY on this trend rule -> made it worse in
//        12 of 12 cells across both assets. See the table below; it is the single
//        most useful thing in this file.
//
// THE 12/12 RESULT, AND WHAT IT MEANS FOR "WIN RATE"
//   Adding a volatility-regime filter to the trend rule RAISED the win rate and
//   DESTROYED the profit factor, every single time (no hysteresis band, so the
//   comparison is like-for-like):
//
//     BTC daily, SMA(100)          trades   win%     PF     total
//       trend only                    50    46.0     5.30   +1299%
//       + vol-expanding filter        91    47.3     1.42     +49%
//       + vol-contracting filter      95    49.5     2.01    +116%
//
//     ETH daily, SMA(100)          trades   win%     PF     total
//       trend only                    60    26.7     3.74    +441%
//       + vol-expanding filter        96    45.8     1.27     -59%
//       + vol-contracting filter     105    52.4     1.62    +185%
//
//   Read the ETH row twice. The filter nearly DOUBLED the win rate (26.7% -> 45.8%)
//   and turned +441% into -59%. The mechanism: the filter chops long trends into
//   more, shorter trades (60 -> 96), each paying the round-trip toll, and it exits
//   during exactly the conditions where the few enormous winners accrue. Trend
//   following earns its money from a small number of very large wins; anything that
//   cuts those short raises the hit rate and lowers the expectancy.
//
//   So: a LOW win rate here is not a flaw to be fixed. A high win rate is
//   purchasable at any time — by small targets against wide stops, or by filtering —
//   and it costs money every time. Judge this by profit factor and expectancy.
//
// MEASURED PERFORMANCE OF THE ACTUAL SHIPPED DEFAULT (SMA 100, 2% band)
//   Same 2019-2026 daily data, 0.54% round-trip cost, signals on confirmed closes:
//
//                    trades  win%    PF    total    maxDD   Sharpe   buy&hold (its DD)
//     BTC              19    47.4   8.08  +2841%   -44.1%    1.02    +1437%  (-76.7%)
//     ETH              23    34.8   8.21  +1576%   -68.3%    0.60    +1318%  (-79.4%)
//
//   Both beat buy-and-hold with a smaller drawdown, both split-halves positive, on
//   the SAME parameters for both assets (not per-asset tuned).
//
// NOW THE PART THAT KEEPS YOU HONEST — READ BEFORE TRADING IT
//   Those PF-of-8 numbers rest on ONE enormous trade per asset:
//
//                    t-stat   p      median trade   biggest win   its share of gross profit
//     BTC             +1.44   0.17      -1.92%        +476%              59%
//     ETH             +1.08   0.29      -7.93%       +1203%              81%
//
//   * NEITHER CLEARS t > 2, never mind this repo's family-wise Sidak bar (~3.0 at
//     the ~20 candidates tried across these sessions). This is NOT a proven edge.
//   * THE MEDIAN TRADE LOSES MONEY on both assets. You should expect most signals
//     to be small losers. The money, in this sample, came from catching one massive
//     trend per cycle and holding it. If you abandon the rule after four losses in
//     a row, you will have paid all the costs and skipped the payoff — that is the
//     single most common way people fail at trend following.
//   * n = 19-23 trades is a small sample. PF 8 at n=19 is a description of this
//     window, not a forecast.
//   * The sample contains one dominant bull market. No walk-forward, no
//     out-of-sample split, no multiple-testing correction.
//   * A 4% band scored HIGHER than the shipped 2% (BTC PF 11.18). It was NOT
//     selected, deliberately: 2% was chosen a priori to match the existing
//     tsmom_paper.py convention, and picking the best-scoring band after seeing the
//     results is the exact overfit this whole exercise was built to avoid.
//
// SIGNALS FIRE ON BAR CLOSE ONLY (confirmed bars). No repainting: every plotted
// signal uses barstate.isconfirmed, so what you see on history is what you would
// have gotten live.
//
// The volatility-regime background is included as a VISUAL ONLY, default OFF. It
// does not gate a single signal. It exists so the thing that was measured harmful
// stays visible and does not get quietly re-added as a filter later.
//
indicator("Trend Signal (Honest)", shorttitle="TrendHonest", overlay=true)

// ── Inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
maLen     = input.int(100, "Trend MA length", minval=5,
             tooltip="100 measured best across BTC and ETH daily. 50 and 200 also work; " +
                     "50 trades more (more cost), 200 trades less (later exits). Not per-asset tuned.")
maType    = input.string("SMA", "MA type", options=["SMA", "EMA"])
bandPct   = input.float(2.0, "Hysteresis band %", minval=0.0, step=0.5,
             tooltip="Price must close this far ABOVE the MA to buy, and this far BELOW to sell. " +
                     "Without it, price hovering on the MA generates a stream of round-trips that " +
                     "pay full cost each time. This is the honest turnover fix, not return tuning.")
showBg    = input.bool(false, "Show volatility-regime background (VISUAL ONLY)",
             tooltip="OFF by default on purpose. Using this as a signal FILTER was measured to " +
                     "raise the win rate and destroy the profit factor in 12 of 12 test cells " +
                     "across BTC and ETH. It is displayed for context, never to gate entries.")
volShort  = input.int(10, "Vol regime: short window", minval=2)
volLong   = input.int(50, "Vol regime: long window", minval=5)

// ── Core rule ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ma      = maType == "EMA" ? ta.ema(close, maLen) : ta.sma(close, maLen)
upper   = ma * (1 + bandPct / 100.0)
lower   = ma * (1 - bandPct / 100.0)

// State machine: long above the upper band, flat below the lower band, hold between.
var bool isLong = false
if close > upper
    isLong := true
else if close < lower
    isLong := false

buySignal  = isLong and not isLong[1]
sellSignal = not isLong and isLong[1]

// ── Volatility regime (display only — never gates a signal) ───────────────────
logret  = math.log(close / close[1])
volS    = ta.stdev(logret, volShort)
volL    = ta.stdev(logret, volLong)
expanding = volS > volL

// ── Plotting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(ma, "Trend MA", color=color.new(color.gray, 0), linewidth=2)
upPlot  = plot(upper, "Upper band", color=color.new(color.gray, 70))
loPlot  = plot(lower, "Lower band", color=color.new(color.gray, 70))
fill(upPlot, loPlot, color=color.new(color.gray, 92), title="Hysteresis band")

barcolor(isLong ? color.new(color.teal, 40) : color.new(color.gray, 70))

bgcolor(showBg ? (expanding ? color.new(color.orange, 92) : color.new(color.blue, 94)) : na,
        title="Vol regime (visual only)")

plotshape(buySignal and barstate.isconfirmed, title="BUY", location=location.belowbar,
          style=shape.labelup, color=color.new(color.teal, 0), textcolor=color.white,
          text="BUY", size=size.small)
plotshape(sellSignal and barstate.isconfirmed, title="SELL", location=location.abovebar,
          style=shape.labeldown, color=color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor=color.white,
          text="SELL", size=size.small)

// ── Alerts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(buySignal,  title="BUY  — trend turned up",
               message="Trend Signal: BUY {{ticker}} @ {{close}} (closed above trend band)")
alertcondition(sellSignal, title="SELL — trend turned down",
               message="Trend Signal: SELL {{ticker}} @ {{close}} (closed below trend band)")

// ── On-chart status ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var table info = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 3, border_width=1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(info, 0, 0, isLong ? "POSITION: LONG" : "POSITION: CASH",
               bgcolor=isLong ? color.new(color.teal, 20) : color.new(color.gray, 30),
               text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal)
    table.cell(info, 0, 1, str.format("trend MA({0}) {1,number,#.##}", maLen, ma),
               text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(info, 0, 2, "win rate is LOW by design — judge by PF",
               text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny)
